    "body": "This PR does 2 things:\r\n1. Fixes a multi-gpu error in mk\r\n2. Adds mi300_2 mirror to run multi-gpu mk tests\r\n\r\n## Why\r\n\r\nRunning `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 pytest tests/kernels/moe/test_modular_kernel_combinations.py -k \"aiter\"` on an MI300 (2-GPU) box, `test_modular_kernel_combinations_multigpu[...]` died with:\r\n\r\n```\r\nAttributeError: 'types.SimpleNamespace' object has no attribute 'sleep_mode_offload_cudagraph'\r\n```\r\n\r\n`tests/kernels/moe/modular_kernel_tools/common.py` fakes `vllm_config.model_config` as a bare `SimpleNamespace(enforce_eager=True, is_moe=True)`. #59160 later added `VllmConfig.use_cumem_cudagraph_pool`, which reads `model_config.sleep_mode_offload_cudagraph` / `.enable_sleep_mode` / `.sleep_mode_backend` — fields the stub predates. That property is evaluated in `CudaCommunicator.__init__` whenever a `GroupCoordinator` with `world_size > 1` is built under `set_current_vllm_config`, which the multi-GPU DP test path does.\r\n\r\nThis fixes the stub by adding the three fields with the same defaults as real `ModelConfig` (`False`, `False`, `\"cumem\"`).\r\n\r\n## Why this wasn't caught by existing CI\r\n\r\nThe only AMD CI job covering this file, `\":amd: (MI300) MoE Kernels Shard %N\"`, runs on the single-GPU `mi300_1` agent pool. `test_modular_kernel_combinations_multigpu` always needs `world_size=2`, so it self-skips via its own `current_platform.device_count() < world_size` check before ever reaching the broken code path — the job shows green while never actually exercising the multi-GPU combinations.\r\n\r\nThis is the same bug class as #53840 / #53925 (ROCm CI jobs under-provisioned relative to a test's declared GPU requirement), but this specific instance wasn't in that audit's list — their scan matched the standard `\"Need at least N GPUs to run the test.\"` skip message, while this test uses a differently-worded custom message (`\"Not enough GPUs available to run, got ... expected ...\"`), so it didn't show up in their log grep.\r\n\r\n## What's added\r\n\r\n- `tests/kernels/moe/modular_kernel_tools/common.py`: add the three missing `sleep_mode_*` fields to the `model_config` stub.\r\n- `.buildkite/test-amd.yaml`: new `\":amd: (MI300) MoE Kernels Multi-GPU\"` job on `mi300_2` (`num_gpus: 2`) running just the `-k \"multigpu\"` cases, so they actually execute instead of perpetually skipping. The existing `mi300_1` job now deselects `multigpu` cases (`-k \"not multigpu\"`) so the two jobs don't both claim the same test IDs — mirrors the \"carved out, nothing double-runs\" pattern from #53925.\r\n\r\n## Test commands run and results\r\n\r\nFull suite, MI300 (2 GPUs), before and after the fix:\r\n\r\n```\r\nVLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 pytest -s -v tests/kernels/moe/test_modular_kernel_combinations.py -k \"aiter\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n- Before: `test_modular_kernel_combinations_multigpu[...]` processes died with the `AttributeError` above (see failure traceback in PR context).\r\n- After: `54 passed, 6 skipped, 21 deselected` (skips are pre-existing/expected — mxfp4 unsupported here, and known AITER×DeepEP-HT illegal-memory-access cases tracked in #57029).\r\n\r\nAlso spot-checked individually:\r\n- `test_aiter_moe_token_padding_garbage_rows[single_nan-unquantized]` — PASSED\r\n- `test_modular_kernel_combinations_multigpu[2048-1024-32-dtype1-None-MoEActivation.SILU-DeepEPHTPrepareAndFinalize-AiterExperts-2]` — PASSED (previously crashed)\r\n\r\nThis change doesn't affect model output/accuracy, so no model eval was run.\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
